WEBVTT

01:01.561 --> 01:03.980
So,
you saw him in the elevator.

01:04.064 --> 01:07.650
And you stole the key from the office
just because you didn't like him?

01:08.359 --> 01:09.694
Hey!

01:09.778 --> 01:12.614
How could you trash his place
just because he ignored you? Huh?

01:12.697 --> 01:13.948
Hey!

01:14.032 --> 01:18.661
And how can you do this to my face just
for playing with an extinguisher? Huh?

01:18.745 --> 01:20.371
I thought you were his friend.

01:20.455 --> 01:22.373
-Sorry.
-My friend? What?

01:22.457 --> 01:23.625
Take it easy.

01:24.459 --> 01:26.294
-Aah.
-Who you talking about? Huh?

01:26.795 --> 01:28.755
What, with this asshole?
Are you kidding me?

01:28.838 --> 01:32.675
I'm not friends with this pathetic loser.
There's no soul in his eyes. Eh?

01:33.176 --> 01:35.887
What about him? You mean he reported me?

01:35.970 --> 01:38.640
Don't be an idiot. He ran away.

01:40.016 --> 01:42.185
Ran away? Why?

01:44.604 --> 01:46.523
That's what I'm asking you.

01:46.606 --> 01:47.899
There's the murderer.

01:49.275 --> 01:51.194
Then the guy who destroyed evidence.

01:54.280 --> 01:55.657
And the runaway.

01:57.117 --> 02:01.371
A KILLER PARADOX

02:25.979 --> 02:27.105
Here's the thing.

02:29.524 --> 02:31.526
When people get old and they get sick,

02:33.153 --> 02:35.613
guess what's the first thing
they run out of?

02:38.908 --> 02:41.119
You will run out of any sort of tolerance.

02:45.415 --> 02:48.459
You suddenly can't seem
to tolerate certain things.

02:50.420 --> 02:52.338
Things you easily could in the past.

02:57.177 --> 02:58.219
Aah…

03:00.221 --> 03:01.598
Certain days,

03:03.558 --> 03:04.434
you might

03:05.560 --> 03:08.313
think the world is swarming
with disgusting vermin.

03:09.147 --> 03:10.148
Hmm?

03:12.734 --> 03:13.985
And other days,

03:15.528 --> 03:16.446
you might

03:18.114 --> 03:20.033
think you could murder anyone you see…

03:23.620 --> 03:24.913
and it'd be good.

03:40.929 --> 03:43.348
Ah shit. Look at this.

03:43.848 --> 03:45.725
I can't fix this.

03:46.434 --> 03:47.560
I just can't.

04:01.741 --> 04:03.618
LEE TANG
CURRENT LOCATION: UNKNOWN

04:05.787 --> 04:09.165
JOONGAM SERVICE AREA

04:12.835 --> 04:14.003
Hmm?

04:14.087 --> 04:16.506
I thought
you would give me a call.

04:18.258 --> 04:19.342
What's the matter?

04:19.884 --> 04:21.511
I'm just…

04:22.303 --> 04:24.305
…frustrated about this whole situation.

04:26.266 --> 04:28.309
Detective Park is saying
to continue to rest,

04:28.393 --> 04:29.894
saying that I'm overzealous.

04:30.561 --> 04:32.438
Right, just cut to the chase already.

04:32.939 --> 04:35.525
I saw on TV
that Ha Sang-min murdered Choi Gyeong-a.

04:36.109 --> 04:38.152
Do I have to learn this
through the news now?

04:38.236 --> 04:40.363
Why haven't you been telling me anything?
I mean--

04:40.947 --> 04:44.742
What, so now it's my job to keep you up
to date with everything that's goin' on?

04:44.826 --> 04:47.912
That's not it. But shouldn't I be
out there doing something?

04:47.996 --> 04:50.623
You said the employee
who ran away was Lee Tang.

04:50.707 --> 04:54.377
I think the explosion was also his doing,
and Ha Sang-min's death too.

04:54.460 --> 04:56.462
You have any evidence he did it?

04:56.546 --> 04:58.089
We haven't found any proof.

04:58.923 --> 05:01.634
Ah, come on!
Then who else could it be?

05:02.302 --> 05:06.556
Just because you believe that he did it
doesn't mean he actually did. Huh?

05:07.056 --> 05:09.809
Stop lashing out at everyone else
just because you got hurt.

05:09.892 --> 05:11.394
Just give it a rest.

05:11.477 --> 05:12.478
Detective Jang.

05:13.438 --> 05:14.689
I saw that bastard.

05:16.607 --> 05:17.608
I'm certain.

05:18.276 --> 05:20.737
I only got a glance at him,
so I didn't know at first.

05:20.820 --> 05:22.322
That's why I didn't tell you.

05:23.906 --> 05:25.908
I think it's the guy you couldn't catch.

05:29.495 --> 05:31.080
How do you even know about him?

05:33.499 --> 05:35.084
Have you been snooping around?

05:35.168 --> 05:37.545
I'm sorry, sir,
but I looked through the files.

05:38.463 --> 05:41.841
Regardless, we know that Roh Bin
and Lee Tang are working together.

05:41.924 --> 05:44.802
We need to do something. Anything.
We could dig into Roh Bin--

05:44.886 --> 05:46.888
Lee Tang or Roh Bin or whoever the hell,

05:46.971 --> 05:49.515
I'll go after them,
so stop whining and stay put.

05:49.599 --> 05:51.434
I mean, I'm not whining right now.

05:51.517 --> 05:52.769
I will catch them.

05:54.937 --> 05:55.813
All right.

06:00.151 --> 06:02.779
If you're here to do
your duties as a son, huh,

06:03.529 --> 06:05.114
then take those calls outside.

06:06.908 --> 06:10.286
You said that you never
wanted to be like your father.

06:10.787 --> 06:11.621
Now,

06:12.246 --> 06:15.458
do you really think that
your behavior is any different than his?

06:18.795 --> 06:22.006
His blood pressure and breathing
are back to normal now.

06:22.757 --> 06:25.551
We should keep an eye on him
for a couple of days.

06:25.635 --> 06:27.637
I see. Thank you.

06:28.930 --> 06:30.973
And this is what I told you about.

06:33.768 --> 06:36.562
Take however much time you need to…

06:36.646 --> 06:38.648
to discuss this between the two of you.

06:39.315 --> 06:43.027
I hope you can consider his delicate
condition and make a careful decision.

06:43.111 --> 06:45.530
FAMILY'S CONSENT TO WITHDRAW
LIFE-SUSTAINING TREATMENT

06:45.613 --> 06:49.450
When he gets put on a ventilator
to begin life-sustaining treatment,

06:50.118 --> 06:52.954
the patient's quality of life
will decrease dramatically.

06:56.457 --> 06:57.667
And when you are ready,

06:58.334 --> 07:03.506
you can sign a DNR or DNI on his behalf
to refuse resuscitation or intubation.

07:24.152 --> 07:25.111
Excuse me.

07:31.576 --> 07:32.493
Hey, sir?

07:34.078 --> 07:35.371
What are you doing?

07:35.872 --> 07:36.831
Huh? What?

07:39.417 --> 07:40.334
Me?

07:41.002 --> 07:42.503
You were groping my leg.

07:44.464 --> 07:46.424
What? What are you talking about?

07:46.507 --> 07:48.926
You just groped my leg.

07:49.010 --> 07:50.678
What are you talking about?

07:50.761 --> 07:53.306
-I fell asleep when I got on.
-She said he groped her.

07:53.389 --> 07:55.349
-Wow.
-What are you talking about?

07:55.433 --> 07:56.851
You're being ridiculous.

07:57.935 --> 08:00.980
-You touched my leg under your briefcase!
-I fell asleep as soon as I got on!

08:01.772 --> 08:03.357
Do you have proof? Huh?

08:04.108 --> 08:06.027
Did anyone see me touch her?

08:06.611 --> 08:08.905
Did anyone take a photo? Did you see it?

08:08.988 --> 08:11.157
-Did anyone see it?
-See? Nobody did.

08:16.996 --> 08:17.955
Hey!

08:18.456 --> 08:21.375
-Oh, hello, sir! Hey.
-Look who it is.

08:33.721 --> 08:34.931
Oppa.

08:35.765 --> 08:37.600
Don't you have exams tomorrow?

08:38.518 --> 08:39.977
Oh, yeah.

08:40.061 --> 08:42.480
I gave it some thought, and

08:43.439 --> 08:46.359
well, my grades are…

08:47.860 --> 08:49.570
They're beyond saving, so…

08:49.654 --> 08:52.073
so I thought, "Why stress?"

08:52.156 --> 08:54.367
I can retake in summer.

08:55.076 --> 08:56.160
Yeah, I guess…

08:57.495 --> 08:59.455
Huh. Uh…

09:02.792 --> 09:04.126
What's your plan today, then?

09:05.086 --> 09:06.128
Huh?

09:08.506 --> 09:10.091
I said, what are you gonna do?

09:11.926 --> 09:13.511
YOU MUST FACE REALITY TO KNOW WHAT TO DO

09:13.594 --> 09:15.972
If you must face reality
to know what to do,

09:17.181 --> 09:18.266
then I won't do anything.

09:21.269 --> 09:23.104
K.O.!

09:24.021 --> 09:26.232
The best way
to dig your head out of the sand

09:26.315 --> 09:31.070
is not by facing reality
but by doing mental gymnastics.

10:00.808 --> 10:05.021
Hey, why do you have so much stuff
all packed in this tiny place?

10:05.646 --> 10:07.857
Cameras, listening devices…

10:07.940 --> 10:09.692
Hmm? How many?

10:10.359 --> 10:13.112
How did you get in here?

10:13.195 --> 10:14.572
How do you think?

10:15.573 --> 10:17.199
I used the front door.

10:17.700 --> 10:19.452
You told me the passcode.

10:26.834 --> 10:27.960
You've lost weight.

10:28.461 --> 10:29.587
Hey.

10:30.254 --> 10:31.756
You know how it goes.

10:33.215 --> 10:35.343
I go on boats to avoid the crackdown.

10:35.426 --> 10:38.512
You keep going in circles.
Bah-bah-bah-bah-bah. Same thing.

10:39.472 --> 10:40.848
Yeah.

10:40.931 --> 10:41.807
Weight loss?

10:42.391 --> 10:43.726
That just happens.

10:44.977 --> 10:46.562
We shoulda been there together.

10:47.188 --> 10:49.732
The gas explosion was you?

10:52.985 --> 10:54.737
So do you still play, uh,

10:55.780 --> 10:57.406
heroes these days?

10:59.742 --> 11:00.868
Back then…

11:02.745 --> 11:05.790
you used to call me
the hero of this generation.

11:05.873 --> 11:07.541
-Right?
-You're no hero!

11:13.422 --> 11:14.423
Ow!

11:15.925 --> 11:18.678
You know, you're the one
who taught me all this stuff.

11:19.553 --> 11:22.264
Hey! You little brat!

11:22.348 --> 11:25.142
I quit because I got fucking tired

11:25.226 --> 11:26.769
of playing along with you.

11:32.024 --> 11:34.985
Anyway, this isn't why I'm here,

11:35.069 --> 11:37.905
but I looked into some stuff
while I was waiting for you.

11:38.406 --> 11:40.741
Yeah, I found some interesting stuff.

11:43.077 --> 11:45.162
The new guy that you got working for you.

11:46.330 --> 11:47.623
Let me meet him.

11:48.874 --> 11:50.459
I'm looking for him,

11:51.502 --> 11:52.670
but he's off the radar.

12:04.056 --> 12:05.766
Hmm.

12:08.352 --> 12:09.979
You're not lying.

12:16.527 --> 12:18.863
Goodness, is this my fault?

12:19.488 --> 12:21.866
Well, he is a funny one.

12:22.575 --> 12:26.912
I said hey. I guess maybe I scared him.
He ran off, huh?

12:26.996 --> 12:29.498
Ran away like a little rat. Huh!

12:29.582 --> 12:31.250
Why would he bolt like that?

12:31.751 --> 12:33.544
No way for a man to behave.

12:35.588 --> 12:37.173
All right. Let's do this, then.

12:38.132 --> 12:40.760
You're going to find him in the end, hmm?

12:41.469 --> 12:44.722
When you do,
set up a meeting and let me know.

12:45.389 --> 12:48.642
Somewhere we can talk. Somewhere private.

12:49.268 --> 12:51.854
Aaah! Minerva. Minerva Coffee.

12:52.438 --> 12:53.314
Love it there.

13:01.322 --> 13:05.117
Oh, and, uh,
let me borrow this book.

13:05.201 --> 13:06.368
CRIME AND PUNISHMENT

13:06.452 --> 13:07.995
Hey, but it's not mine.

13:08.871 --> 13:09.872
Hey, hey…

13:10.539 --> 13:11.999
Stop being a weirdo about it.

13:13.167 --> 13:16.295
Who would even lock that away?

13:17.046 --> 13:18.714
A borrowed book in a safe?

13:20.341 --> 13:22.927
Ah, there's this strange stain

13:24.011 --> 13:26.013
in the middle of the book too.

13:27.598 --> 13:30.726
-You're such a little klutz.
-Ow.

13:34.647 --> 13:37.024
Round one. Fight.

13:50.913 --> 13:52.164
K.O… K.O…

13:52.248 --> 13:53.374
K.O…

13:53.999 --> 13:55.668
K.O… K.O…

13:56.252 --> 13:58.003
You lose… You lose…

14:02.675 --> 14:05.636
He's that important? The kid?

14:06.262 --> 14:08.013
Continue?

14:08.097 --> 14:09.890
Nine, eight,

14:10.391 --> 14:12.226
seven, six,

14:12.810 --> 14:14.478
five, four,

14:15.145 --> 14:17.731
three, two, one.

14:18.482 --> 14:20.067
Game over.

14:31.704 --> 14:32.580
What?

15:27.509 --> 15:28.969
-Huh?
-Damn it.

15:32.222 --> 15:33.432
What the hell?

15:38.354 --> 15:39.939
Fuck. Damn it.

15:40.981 --> 15:42.024
Fuck.

15:45.819 --> 15:47.196
Who the hell are you, huh?

15:47.696 --> 15:49.615
I'm a cop, motherfucker.

15:50.532 --> 15:53.369
Why is a cop moving alone?
Something's fishy.

15:54.161 --> 15:56.789
-You son of a bitch.
-Hey, now.

15:56.872 --> 15:58.374
Let me go, you motherfucker!

16:11.428 --> 16:14.515
-He says he'll only talk to you. Go on in.
-Yes, sir.

16:15.349 --> 16:17.643
Do we just let him sit there, sir?

16:19.019 --> 16:21.146
Hey. Go ahead.

16:21.230 --> 16:23.065
Ugh, what do we do with him?

16:23.148 --> 16:25.734
What else can we do?
We have to follow procedure.

16:26.902 --> 16:31.198
I heard thuds outside my door,
so I went out to see who it was.

16:31.865 --> 16:33.909
The detective was on the ground,

16:34.702 --> 16:35.619
unconscious.

16:36.954 --> 16:38.664
I didn't see who beat him up.

16:39.623 --> 16:42.334
That's the story I told
the other detectives when I came in,

16:42.418 --> 16:43.252
but I--

16:43.335 --> 16:44.586
-Hey.
-Yeah?

16:48.257 --> 16:50.217
Just cut to the chase or I'll kill you.

16:51.552 --> 16:55.889
Yeah, that's why I brought you
several of these documents.

17:01.478 --> 17:03.605
I didn't know he was back in Korea.

17:04.982 --> 17:07.860
I thought I'd never hear
from that guy ever again.

17:13.615 --> 17:14.700
It was Song Chon.

17:15.659 --> 17:17.369
He's the one who did that to Detective An.

17:17.453 --> 17:18.620
PERSONAL DETAILS
SONG CHON

17:20.205 --> 17:22.708
He should be somewhere in Seoul.

17:24.084 --> 17:26.920
The gas explosion in Busan was
his doing as well.

17:27.004 --> 17:28.005
Where were you?

17:29.339 --> 17:30.424
What the fuck?

17:35.471 --> 17:36.346
Hey!

17:37.097 --> 17:37.973
Hey!

17:39.183 --> 17:41.310
Keep your fuckin' eyes open, will you?

17:41.935 --> 17:43.312
You should be on the sidewalk.

17:43.395 --> 17:46.315
-What? You almost ran us over. Asshole.
-Oppa.

17:46.398 --> 17:47.900
-Let it go.
-You must be blind.

17:47.983 --> 17:49.860
-Driving this piece of shit.
-Why bother?

17:49.943 --> 17:51.904
-That's enough.
-I'm not fucking done.

17:51.987 --> 17:54.364
-You piece of shit!
-Oppa, come on.

17:55.741 --> 17:59.078
-Get back to work, fuckhead.
-You're wasting your time, okay?

17:59.161 --> 18:00.537
Let's go.

18:06.710 --> 18:10.756
It's the file I gave you before,
with some updates.

18:10.839 --> 18:12.257
DIRECTOR PARK HYEONG-JIN

18:12.341 --> 18:17.888
I've also added the unaccounted-for murder
cases that I told you about earlier.

18:23.894 --> 18:26.021
Haven't we gone through this before?

18:27.898 --> 18:29.691
You came to me a few years ago.

18:30.734 --> 18:34.446
You gave me stacks of files saying I'm
the only one who can catch Song Chon.

18:35.155 --> 18:35.989
That right?

18:36.907 --> 18:38.867
Well, you're the one who lost him.

18:39.743 --> 18:42.830
I could've caught him before if you'd
brought me everything like now.

18:42.913 --> 18:44.498
Isn't that your forte?

18:45.833 --> 18:49.670
Testing people without fully committing,
and jumping ship when it goes south?

18:51.130 --> 18:52.881
Isn't that what you're doing
with Lee Tang?

18:56.218 --> 18:57.594
Tang is different.

18:58.178 --> 19:00.889
And he's got nothing to do with this case.

19:04.268 --> 19:05.769
Aah. Hah!

19:10.440 --> 19:11.650
How is he different?

19:14.820 --> 19:17.072
Listen, I'll explain everything later.

19:18.740 --> 19:20.909
Can you please just help me out this once?

19:20.993 --> 19:23.579
If you do, I swear I'll tell you
everything you wanna know.

19:23.662 --> 19:25.289
You wanna make a deal with me?

19:26.665 --> 19:29.501
That's right.
It's time that you get your revenge.

19:30.544 --> 19:33.839
Who do you think you are, telling
a police detective to get his revenge?

19:37.217 --> 19:38.135
Listen.

19:39.428 --> 19:42.514
I have no intention of working
with a fucking nerd like you. Take this.

19:42.598 --> 19:43.891
Get lost, hmm?

19:45.350 --> 19:48.020
And don't go getting
yourself killed messing around.

19:49.438 --> 19:50.606
You have to lie low.

19:51.899 --> 19:52.816
Got it?

19:57.821 --> 19:58.739
What's going on?

20:01.241 --> 20:05.162
Yong-jae says he saw him
on the day of the gas explosion.

20:05.245 --> 20:07.539
-He might actually be telling the truth.
-Hey.

20:07.623 --> 20:09.541
The captain lost his job
because of that punk.

20:09.625 --> 20:11.668
-That's not my fault.
-And Yong-jae is in a coma.

20:11.752 --> 20:13.086
I know! What do you want me to do?

20:13.170 --> 20:15.214
-You can't get involved with that guy!
-No choice!

20:15.297 --> 20:17.758
My hands are tied with the suspension.
Huh?

20:21.094 --> 20:22.346
You do what you gotta do.

20:22.429 --> 20:25.015
-And I'll do what I gotta do.
-Wait, stop. Nan-gam!

20:29.061 --> 20:30.020
Who's that?

20:30.103 --> 20:33.690
The detective who got suspended.
Nan-gam. That's him.

20:45.744 --> 20:46.745
You guys

20:48.080 --> 20:49.623
are just like weeds.

20:50.916 --> 20:53.335
Your roots are so deep,

20:54.586 --> 20:56.838
it's impossible
to get rid of you entirely.

21:00.133 --> 21:01.301
In the morning,

21:02.344 --> 21:03.679
everyone is exhausted

21:04.388 --> 21:05.430
and tired.

21:06.723 --> 21:09.601
You just had to stand
in the road and chat away, huh?

21:10.978 --> 21:12.479
And disobey traffic laws.

21:14.064 --> 21:16.692
And talk back to elders.

21:16.775 --> 21:19.194
-Huh?
-I'm so sorry.

21:19.278 --> 21:20.988
-That right?
-I'm so sorry.

21:21.780 --> 21:23.240
I'm so sorry, sir.

21:27.119 --> 21:29.621
I guess, if you think about it,

21:30.539 --> 21:31.915
it's not your fault, is it?

21:31.999 --> 21:33.292
Hmm?

21:33.375 --> 21:34.501
When you were little,

21:35.419 --> 21:37.838
your parents didn't scold you
for running around

21:38.880 --> 21:41.049
and causing a commotion in public, huh?

21:41.633 --> 21:44.553
You learned you could get your way
by being obnoxious.

21:44.636 --> 21:47.014
But that's the fast track
to ruining your kid.

21:53.645 --> 21:54.479
Now,

21:55.272 --> 21:57.774
isn't it great to see
what you've been doing wrong?

21:59.651 --> 22:02.446
Eh… I'll let you go.

22:02.529 --> 22:04.114
But you need to promise me

22:04.614 --> 22:07.784
that from now on, you're gonna
live the life of a model citizen.

22:10.037 --> 22:12.873
-Thank you. Thank you.
-All right.

22:12.956 --> 22:14.875
Thank you so much.

22:17.169 --> 22:18.420
Do you have a pen?

22:20.213 --> 22:22.257
-Pen. Pen.
-I don't, I'm sorry.

22:22.341 --> 22:24.259
-Ballpoint.
-I don't have one.

22:25.177 --> 22:26.386
Oh no.

22:27.888 --> 22:31.266
You're a student. You should be
carrying one around with you.

22:31.350 --> 22:34.102
It's… I'm in art school.

22:36.688 --> 22:39.399
-Oh, that's a bummer.
-What?

22:39.483 --> 22:42.986
If you're in art school,
you might draw my face one day.

22:43.070 --> 22:44.029
No, please.

22:44.112 --> 22:46.948
I'm a terrible artist. I really am.

22:47.032 --> 22:50.994
I went to a lousy university
in the countryside.

22:51.078 --> 22:53.789
I'm begging you, don't kill me.

22:55.916 --> 22:57.542
Art schools are expensive.

22:58.668 --> 23:01.171
You should be able to draw
if you went to an art school.

23:01.880 --> 23:04.925
Two citizens
who were having a meal at a restaurant

23:05.008 --> 23:07.594
performed CPR on a person who collapsed.

23:07.677 --> 23:09.930
-They were able to save a precious life.
-Hmm.

23:10.013 --> 23:12.224
They turned out to be new police recruits.

23:12.307 --> 23:13.475
They are Officer Kim

23:13.558 --> 23:16.686
from the Central Precinct
of Gyeongbuk Gucheon Police Station,

23:16.770 --> 23:20.774
and Officer Shin from the Central Precinct
of Seoul Dangjeong Police Station.

23:20.857 --> 23:24.986
The two were eating in a restaurant
in Gangseo-gu, Seoul, on the 21st

23:25.070 --> 23:28.198
when they saw the waitress collapse
while serving food.

23:28.782 --> 23:31.868
They immediately
administered aid and saved her life.

23:32.619 --> 23:35.705
In the urgent situation,
Officer Kim called emergency services

23:35.789 --> 23:38.750
while Officer Shin began performing CPR.

23:38.834 --> 23:42.003
The unconscious employee
woke up after two minutes.

23:42.504 --> 23:44.673
The two officers
who immediately came to her aid

23:44.756 --> 23:47.217
joined the police force at the same time,

23:47.300 --> 23:49.761
and they had received
their training together.

23:50.387 --> 23:52.764
Security camera footage went viral online

23:52.848 --> 23:55.809
when it was revealed
that the two were new recruits.

23:56.351 --> 24:00.397
The waitress who collapsed regained
consciousness after receiving CPR

24:00.480 --> 24:02.732
and was treated at the hospital afterward.

24:03.817 --> 24:06.611
The two received commendation
from the Commissioner General.

24:17.372 --> 24:19.374
The man seems taken aback and flees.

24:19.458 --> 24:22.335
The victim's friend chases him,
but he manages to escape.

24:22.419 --> 24:26.798
The authorities identified him as Lee,
a criminal wanted for attempted murder.

24:27.674 --> 24:30.927
The victim, Mr. Kim,
died on the way to the hospital.

24:31.428 --> 24:33.221
WANTED CRIMINAL FLEES
AFTER A STABBING RAMPAGE

24:33.305 --> 24:36.475
The police are expanding their search
in order to find Lee, who escaped.

24:37.100 --> 24:39.853
They have made a request
for an arrest warrant…

24:49.488 --> 24:52.782
I CAUSED A SCENE, INSULTED MY ELDERS,
NEGLECTED STUDIES, DID DRUGS - HYUNG JI-SU

25:02.292 --> 25:04.711
FAMILY'S CONSENT TO WITHDRAW
LIFE-SUSTAINING TREATMENT

25:04.794 --> 25:07.214
SIGNED: JANG NAN-GAM

25:31.571 --> 25:32.614
Get your rest.

25:44.209 --> 25:45.210
Yeah?

25:45.293 --> 25:47.295
-Detective Jang Nan-gam?
-Yes.

25:47.379 --> 25:50.090
I'm Moon Myeong-jun, the new captain.

25:50.173 --> 25:51.216
Are you home?

25:52.092 --> 25:56.805
I heard that you were the one
who knows the most, uh…

25:56.888 --> 25:58.598
…about Song Chon.

26:00.559 --> 26:04.104
-Is that what they said?
-I also heard that it was personal.

26:05.772 --> 26:07.190
It kind of was, I suppose.

26:08.024 --> 26:10.277
Hey. It's great to have motivation.

26:11.861 --> 26:13.113
This isn't right.

26:13.863 --> 26:17.951
I thought you'd have his case files
glued on every wall of your house in here.

26:19.202 --> 26:20.745
Like in the movies.

26:21.746 --> 26:22.914
Sorry to ask you…

26:23.582 --> 26:26.418
is there a reason that you stopped by?

26:30.463 --> 26:32.549
Well, I think…

26:34.718 --> 26:35.802
this tip-off,

26:37.137 --> 26:39.347
I find it quite credible, to be honest.

26:43.351 --> 26:44.603
And…

26:45.854 --> 26:46.813
this here.

26:47.647 --> 26:49.816
This Mapo Station case
was just filed today.

26:55.822 --> 26:58.867
I think it's the same MO.
What do you think?

27:04.956 --> 27:05.999
It's a possibility.

27:07.876 --> 27:11.212
He killed the wrong person
this time, however.

27:12.422 --> 27:15.342
You know the famous case
with Gajok Construction, right?

27:16.092 --> 27:17.260
Yes. I do.

27:17.344 --> 27:19.929
It's now called Buyeon Construction.

27:21.056 --> 27:22.641
This is the chairman's granddaughter.

27:24.684 --> 27:27.437
And apparently,
a special promotion is on the line

27:27.520 --> 27:29.522
for whoever is able to solve this case.

27:33.401 --> 27:34.402
Detective Jang.

27:36.321 --> 27:38.698
Help me. Help me catch my break.

27:41.451 --> 27:42.911
Come back to work tomorrow.

27:44.120 --> 27:45.580
-Tomorrow?
-Mm-hmm.

27:46.081 --> 27:49.334
Besides, we can't just let this monster
wander around at large.

28:21.157 --> 28:22.951
NEW ACTIVITY FROM LEE TANG

28:27.163 --> 28:28.248
ME

28:28.331 --> 28:29.499
LEE TANG - ONLINE

28:29.582 --> 28:30.417
HEROES

28:31.835 --> 28:34.671
Oh, um…
I, uh, have to take this. I'm sorry.

28:35.547 --> 28:37.966
I'll be right back, okay? I'm sorry.

28:57.485 --> 29:00.113
MY DEEPEST CONDOLENCES

29:00.196 --> 29:01.823
Don't worry about the book.

29:01.906 --> 29:05.910
There's a plan A, B, C, D.
Don't worry, okay? Look, I've got this.

29:06.411 --> 29:09.080
I'll clean this up.
So you just keep lying low.

29:09.164 --> 29:10.790
Don't change the subject.

29:13.418 --> 29:15.086
What kind of man is this guy?

29:15.670 --> 29:16.588
Uh…

29:18.965 --> 29:21.009
Who the hell are you? Come on!

29:24.137 --> 29:25.346
Don't!

29:25.430 --> 29:26.765
Oh God!

29:33.396 --> 29:35.857
I thought he was like you at first.

29:36.900 --> 29:39.986
Because he wanted to change the world.

29:40.779 --> 29:42.864
You're exactly what
this world needs right now.

29:43.448 --> 29:47.702
So how about we join forces,
and then bring justice to the world?

30:08.473 --> 30:11.726
But I was very, very wrong.

30:14.103 --> 30:17.315
So it's my responsibility to fix this.

30:20.610 --> 30:21.611
Let me meet him.

30:23.488 --> 30:25.573
Huh? Really?

30:30.537 --> 30:32.330
The situation's been changed.

30:35.208 --> 30:37.252
LUXURY KARAOKE

30:39.879 --> 30:41.256
I REPENT WITH MY DEATH

30:41.339 --> 30:43.633
I CAUSED A COMMOTION AT A RESTAURANT

30:43.716 --> 30:45.510
I, KIM WON-JONG, SCAMMED MY FRIENDS

30:51.766 --> 30:53.601
ROH BIN: TANG WANTS TO MEET YOU TOO

31:15.582 --> 31:16.499
Huh.

31:18.209 --> 31:19.210
Well, hi.

31:21.588 --> 31:24.591
I heard that
you were interested in meeting me.

31:25.967 --> 31:27.010
Yeah.

31:28.136 --> 31:32.515
You're much more courageous
than you look, huh? Ten points for you!

31:33.349 --> 31:34.434
Right.

31:35.602 --> 31:37.437
I'm gonna give you some directions.

31:37.520 --> 31:38.980
MINERVA COFFEE SHOP

31:39.063 --> 31:40.690
So listen up, okay?

31:41.816 --> 31:43.860
It's better if we, uh…

31:44.569 --> 31:47.405
meet somewhere nicer than a coffee shop.

31:47.488 --> 31:48.364
Huh?

31:48.448 --> 31:50.617
LEE TANG
SEOUL, MAPO-GU, SUNGSINCHUN-DONG, 31-3

31:50.700 --> 31:51.701
What is it?

31:54.996 --> 31:57.582
-Hey, hey, move.
-Sorry, sorry, sorry.

31:59.667 --> 32:02.420
Yeah, yeah.
That's the place. That's it. All right.

32:03.004 --> 32:05.715
Now, come to the second floor, okay?

32:05.798 --> 32:07.008
ROH BIN
DECLINE CALL

32:07.091 --> 32:08.885
Come right in.

32:08.968 --> 32:09.886
HAWAII CLUB

32:09.969 --> 32:11.554
You found it. Hah!

32:26.277 --> 32:28.988
HAWAII CLUB

32:45.088 --> 32:47.548
Hey. Over here.

33:05.233 --> 33:06.359
Help yourself.

33:11.489 --> 33:12.782
So, what do you want?

33:14.283 --> 33:15.660
I thought it'd be nice.

33:16.786 --> 33:19.080
We can talk about life now.

33:20.415 --> 33:22.083
We're in the same shoes.

33:23.376 --> 33:24.419
It's not like…

33:25.294 --> 33:28.881
…we can talk about things
to anyone else.

33:29.382 --> 33:31.509
It's frustrating, lonely.

33:32.719 --> 33:33.803
I understand.

33:38.307 --> 33:39.267
You know,

33:39.767 --> 33:42.270
I've been curious about somethin', hmm?

33:43.021 --> 33:44.355
How do you…

33:45.273 --> 33:46.899
how do you pick who dies?

33:48.276 --> 33:49.110
Hmm?

33:49.193 --> 33:50.528
ME

33:50.611 --> 33:52.155
-Turn left here.
-What?

33:52.238 --> 33:53.865
Left on this street! Go now!

33:53.948 --> 33:55.867
Ah, you should've said sooner.

33:56.367 --> 33:58.077
Ah, U-turns are the worst.

33:58.161 --> 34:00.204
Sir, I think
you have to make a U-turn.

34:00.288 --> 34:02.790
-What am I supposed to do?
-Just make a U-turn! There are no cars!

34:02.874 --> 34:05.334
-That's not legal.
-So you follow every fucking law?

34:05.418 --> 34:08.254
-Shut it. I'm not doing that.
-Hey, shut up! Will you just shut up?

34:08.880 --> 34:10.673
Just make a left turn up here, all right?

34:11.758 --> 34:13.134
Little bitch.

34:16.387 --> 34:18.347
Wait, maybe that's too big for a start.

34:20.058 --> 34:22.060
Something easier. Hmm.

34:23.394 --> 34:26.939
I heard that you… get these hunches,
or something.

34:27.899 --> 34:28.775
Wait, what?

34:31.569 --> 34:33.154
Are you normally this quiet?

34:36.199 --> 34:37.658
Answer yes or no.

34:40.119 --> 34:43.164
Do you get, you know, tingles?

34:43.748 --> 34:46.042
Something like that? This jolt?

34:46.125 --> 34:47.126
Huh?

34:54.634 --> 34:55.927
Is this the right place?

34:58.012 --> 34:59.472
I… I'm pretty sure it is.

35:00.473 --> 35:01.474
Get a move on!

35:02.100 --> 35:02.934
Hurry!

35:03.476 --> 35:05.144
-Come on, move!
-Hey, hey!

35:05.228 --> 35:07.355
I'm done with your bullshit. Grab him.

35:10.608 --> 35:12.944
Hey, what are you doing?
Why are you doing this?

35:13.861 --> 35:17.115
I mean, learn to read the room
before you act out.

35:18.074 --> 35:19.033
Yeah?

35:22.078 --> 35:24.288
You're really getting on my nerves.

35:29.127 --> 35:30.795
Aaah!

35:30.878 --> 35:33.506
Hang on. So, it's not like…

35:35.258 --> 35:39.345
you have some kind of special,
uh, superpower, huh?

35:40.513 --> 35:42.473
Where, I mean, you somehow know

35:42.557 --> 35:46.102
all the evil deeds that a person has done
in their entire life

35:46.185 --> 35:47.478
just by touching them?

35:47.562 --> 35:48.729
'Cause that's insane.

35:53.109 --> 35:55.778
Aah. Oh, come on.

35:57.613 --> 35:59.615
Hey, yeah.

36:00.867 --> 36:01.909
This is boring.

36:03.161 --> 36:06.164
Huh? Boy, this is anticlimactic.

36:09.750 --> 36:12.003
HAWAII CLUB

36:20.511 --> 36:21.387
Anyway.

36:23.055 --> 36:25.057
Do you have any questions for me?

36:27.226 --> 36:28.936
Ask me anything. I'll tell you.

36:32.773 --> 36:33.983
Where's my book at?

36:35.818 --> 36:38.613
Ah, the one I borrowed?

36:41.699 --> 36:42.867
I'm not done with it.

36:44.952 --> 36:45.828
Hey.

36:47.121 --> 36:48.664
About Roh Bin, huh?

36:50.875 --> 36:52.126
Don't trust that guy.

36:54.337 --> 36:57.131
If you make a single mistake,

36:58.799 --> 37:00.509
he'll abandon you right away.

37:02.303 --> 37:04.013
Look how he was keeping your book.

37:07.308 --> 37:08.267
Ugh.

37:10.019 --> 37:11.479
Do you wanna work together?

37:12.813 --> 37:13.689
Hmm?

37:14.774 --> 37:16.651
The problem is, I get confused

37:18.277 --> 37:20.821
when I pick who I might kill.

37:20.905 --> 37:23.908
It keeps getting more and more confusing.

37:26.869 --> 37:29.455
I don't care if you mess up, hmm?

37:30.498 --> 37:33.292
There's always collateral damage
for the common good.

37:34.043 --> 37:35.086
Wouldn't you agree?

37:40.800 --> 37:42.802
So much garbage to clean up,

37:43.970 --> 37:45.638
but I don't have much time.

37:46.138 --> 37:48.015
And I'm not as young as I used to be.

37:49.016 --> 37:50.142
Aah!

37:50.226 --> 37:53.020
Well, it's… it's getting quite late.

37:54.397 --> 37:56.565
So think it over and let me know.

37:58.234 --> 38:00.444
Don't make me wait too long, though, pal.

38:03.364 --> 38:06.450
You know what the issue is, huh?

38:07.326 --> 38:11.163
They'll just keep making trouble
if you let them be.

38:48.242 --> 38:49.744
Is this your answer?

38:50.536 --> 38:51.662
Hah.

38:52.330 --> 38:53.789
Oh.

38:53.873 --> 38:56.709
We should always be on alert, right?

38:57.668 --> 38:58.711
Most people…

38:59.754 --> 39:01.339
Eh?

39:01.422 --> 39:03.674
Don't know exactly when they'll die.

39:04.717 --> 39:08.846
That's the reason
assholes like you can get them.

39:08.929 --> 39:10.014
But me,

39:11.182 --> 39:12.475
I'm not one of them.

39:14.060 --> 39:16.145
Huh.

39:17.521 --> 39:18.522
Yeah…

39:19.357 --> 39:21.484
Now you look like
you've come to your senses.

39:22.985 --> 39:26.113
You look so pitiful.

39:26.697 --> 39:28.282
Hmm? Know what?

39:30.117 --> 39:31.577
I've given it some thought.

39:32.078 --> 39:33.579
And you just

39:34.663 --> 39:36.123
don't seem to have any sense

39:36.999 --> 39:38.793
of heroism or responsibility.

39:40.669 --> 39:42.421
Aren't you just a murderer, then?

39:43.547 --> 39:45.007
A murderer that…

39:46.884 --> 39:47.885
deserves to die.

39:51.764 --> 39:52.807
Oh.

39:55.017 --> 39:57.436
Fuck. He caught us, you shithead.

39:58.145 --> 39:59.814
I told you to stay quiet.

39:59.897 --> 40:01.816
I'm sorry, sir.
My legs were cramped.

40:01.899 --> 40:02.733
Yeah, yeah.

40:04.026 --> 40:06.070
Hey! Hey!

40:06.153 --> 40:07.530
We… we're not open.

40:08.531 --> 40:09.907
We're not here to drink.

40:12.368 --> 40:13.661
Then what do you want?

40:15.037 --> 40:16.914
We're here to escort you, sir.

40:17.415 --> 40:18.290
Shall we?

40:21.877 --> 40:23.003
Who's this?

40:23.879 --> 40:25.297
What's with the scrawny kid?

40:25.798 --> 40:28.634
-Do we just let him walk?
-What the hell?

40:50.072 --> 40:50.990
Thanks.

41:01.625 --> 41:03.127
Why did you keep the book?

41:07.173 --> 41:09.091
It wasn't because I didn't trust you.

41:10.968 --> 41:12.428
I had this plan.

41:14.096 --> 41:15.431
But he took the book.

41:16.140 --> 41:17.141
I'm sorry.

41:17.892 --> 41:19.602
I failed you.

41:26.442 --> 41:29.653
But I still have a plan.
Can you just trust me again?

41:37.369 --> 41:38.329
Hyung.

41:47.046 --> 41:48.422
I'm so scared.
